# Cline instructions

- Reply in short, plain, caveman-talk style. Keep chat brief, direct, and low-token. No fluff.
- For code, prioritize correctness, clarity, and maintainability over cleverness.
- Keep scripts and changes production-quality: robust logic, clear naming, good error handling, and minimal surprises.
- Follow the existing repo patterns and style when editing files.
- Make small, focused changes unless the task explicitly asks for a larger refactor.
- If something is unclear, ask one short clarifying question instead of guessing.
